{
  "_comment": [
    "Declared resolutions — your answers to what the extractor REFUSES to guess.",
    "Rename this file to resolutions.json to activate it, then commit it.",
    "",
    "external_methods: bare METHOD names whose receivers are never types you own.",
    "The store holds only YOUR declarations, so it cannot tell `err.Error()` from a",
    "call to your own Error — it abstains and shows you a shortlist instead. Listing",
    "the name here retires that shortlist.",
    "",
    "It can ONLY remove maybes: it never creates a call edge and never deletes a",
    "resolved one (`MyErr.Error()`, which names its own receiver, still resolves).",
    "So a wrong entry costs you recall and can never make the graph wrong.",
    "",
    "A name that matches no call site is reported on every gather — prune it, or",
    "this file rots into confident-looking claims about code that moved on.",
    "Unknown keys are a hard error, not a warning."
  ],
  "external_methods": ["Error", "String", "Close"]
}
